    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0358" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg230"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 172.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Scruggs</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 19,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 74.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 239, of the 2d of
                    October, referring to the proposed establishment by Colombia of custom-houses at
                    Colon and Panama, and detailing your action in the direction of preventing this
                    and providing for the continued freedom of the Isthmian transit.</p>
                <p>Your action is quite consistent with that contemplated by one of the
                    instructions—No. 2, of November 3—just given to the new minister, Mr. Jacob, on
                    the same subject.</p>
                <p>I inclose a copy of that instruction.<anchor n="†" xml:id="d172-f1"/></p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
